WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:06.800
A model can pass every check and still be wrong.

2
00:00:06.800 --> 00:00:12.000
Fast. Always readable. Always the right shape.

3
00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:16.300
The shape of an answer says nothing about its truth.

4
00:00:16.300 --> 00:00:21.300
So: ten real pages, answers written by hand.

5
00:00:21.300 --> 00:00:26.400
Three publish no price at all.

6
00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:31.500
On one, a real price for a different product.

7
00:00:31.500 --> 00:00:35.300
Resisting that is harder than not inventing.

8
00:00:35.300 --> 00:00:40.400
The first score was low. Our fault.

9
00:00:40.400 --> 00:00:45.700
Asked for four facts, it wrote two and stopped.

10
00:00:45.700 --> 00:00:49.500
Silence looked exactly like an honest gap.

11
00:00:49.500 --> 00:00:54.700
Fixed. Now the faulty copy scores ten percent.

12
00:00:54.700 --> 00:01:00.000
The good copy, same speed, scores eighty-seven.

13
00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:04.000
That gap used to be a note somebody had to read.

14
00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:09.100
One failure is worth understanding.

15
00:01:09.100 --> 00:01:14.500
It quoted a price correctly, from the wrong plan.

16
00:01:14.500 --> 00:01:18.300
Nothing invented. That is the hard case.

17
00:01:18.300 --> 00:01:23.400
So the set checks itself first.

18
00:01:23.400 --> 00:01:28.500
Every answer must really be on its page.

19
00:01:28.500 --> 00:01:33.600
One tidy idea was measured and dropped.

20
00:01:33.600 --> 00:01:39.100
Forbidding the bad answer made the good one rarer.

21
00:01:39.100 --> 00:01:42.700
The next faulty model is caught by a test.
